# OptiQuery configuration template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#
# Then paste your key into .env. That file is gitignored; this one is committed,
# so never put a real key here.
#
# The seeder service loads this file via `env_file:`, which means THIS FILE WINS
# over anything already set in your shell or Windows environment. That is
# deliberate: a stale key left in a user profile silently overriding the one you
# can actually see in the repo is a genuinely nasty thing to debug.
#
# The exception is PG_PARALLEL, which is substituted into the postgres services
# rather than passed to a container. Shell substitution *does* prefer the host
# environment, so an exported PG_PARALLEL would override the value below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model provider
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fill in exactly ONE of the keys below. Leave the rest blank.
#
# With OPTIQUERY_PROVIDER unset, app/llm.py auto-detects in this order:
#   anthropic -> gemini -> groq -> cerebras -> openrouter -> github
# Anthropic leads because it is the only path with prompt caching and thinking
# blocks. Set OPTIQUERY_PROVIDER to override, which you need if more than one
# key is present.

# Reference implementation. Pay-as-you-go, not a subscription: $5 minimum.
# A full run over all 4 seed queries costs well under $1 with caching on.
#   https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# RECOMMENDED FREE OPTION. No card required. 1M context, strong tool calling --
# the context matters here because the transcript grows with every observation.
#   https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Free tier, very fast. ~128k context is the binding constraint on a long run.
#   https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Free tier, very fast.
#   https://cloud.cerebras.ai
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# One key, many models. Free models carry a ':free' suffix -- check the model's
# page for tool-calling support before using it, since not all of them have it.
#   https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Free with a GitHub account. Needs a fine-grained PAT with the models scope.
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Force a provider instead of auto-detecting. One of:
#   anthropic | gemini | groq | cerebras | openrouter | github | ollama
# 'ollama' is the only value that needs no key at all -- fully local, no rate
# limits, but slow without a GPU. Pick a model whose card lists tool support.
OPTIQUERY_PROVIDER=

# Override that provider's default model. Model IDs drift faster than anything
# else in this project; if a request 404s, set the current ID here rather than
# editing app/llm.py. Defaults per provider:
#   anthropic  claude-sonnet-4-6
#   gemini     gemini-3.6-flash
#              Verified free-tier alternatives, best first: gemini-3.5-flash,
#              gemini-3-flash-preview, gemini-flash-latest, gemini-3.5-flash-lite.
#              Avoid gemini-2.5-*: it 404s for keys created after Google
#              restricted it. Every *-pro model 429s on the free tier.
#   groq       llama-3.3-70b-versatile
#   cerebras   llama-3.3-70b
#   openrouter meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free
#   github     openai/gpt-4o
#   ollama     qwen3:8b
OPTIQUERY_MODEL=

# Where a local Ollama listens. host.docker.internal reaches your machine from
# inside the container; use http://localhost:11434 when running outside Docker.
OLLAMA_HOST=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both databases run with max_parallel_workers_per_gather=0 so timings are
# single-threaded and comparable. Parallel worker allocation is nondeterministic
# under load and is the largest source of run-to-run variance -- a harness that
# has to detect a 20% improvement cannot afford +/-40% noise. Set to 2 to
# restore stock behaviour, at the cost of noisier benchmarks.
PG_PARALLEL=0

# Shrink the seed data for a faster load. 1.0 is the full 4.75M rows described
# in the README; 0.1 loads a tenth of that. Queries stay slow enough to
# optimise at 0.5 and below that the failure modes start to disappear.
OPTIQUERY_SCALE=1.0
